1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Irene Mary Taylor''' (née '''Hardacre'''; March 7, 1932 – October 16, 2015) was a British tailoress and Traditionalist Catholic religious figure best known for her opposition to the Second Vatican Council and he
2 CONC r spiritual struggles thereafter. Irene Mary organised Latin Masses during the 1970s at her and her husband Derrick's home 222 Longmeanygate near Leyland in Lancashire and she has become known for her Catholic writings. The life s
2 CONC tory of Irene Mary and Derrick Taylor have caused their grandson Cometan to found their Cause for Beatification in 2020.
