1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Priscilla Grinnell Redfield==
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH	1689, Little Compton, Newport County, Rhode Island, USA
2 CONT DEATH	12 Jan 1770 (aged 80–81)
2 CONT BURIAL	Indian River Cemetery, Clinton, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA, MEMORIAL ID 17057193, Photos by Irma & Howard William Sternberg III
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscribed
2 CONT "in Memory of
2 CONT Mre. Pricilla
2 CONT Redfield Wive of
2 CONT Mr. Theophilus
2 CONT Redfield
2 CONT died January 12th
2 CONT A.D. 1770
2 CONT in her 81st
2 CONT year"
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Daniel Grinnell and Lydia Pabodie Grinnell, she was the great granddaughter of John Alden and Priscilla Mullins of the Mayflower. She married Theophilus Redfield on 24 Dec 1706 and settled in Killingworth, Connecticut.
2 CONC  She bore thirteen children, all attaining adulthood and having children of their own. Through this connection, 9/10ths of those today bearing the surname "Redfield" may claim Mayflower descendancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT In Memory of
2 CONT Mrs.. Priscilla
2 CONT Redfield Wife of
2 CONT Mr. Theophilus
2 CONT Redfield
2 CONT died Jan. ye 12th..
2 CONT A.D. 1770
2 CONT In her 81st.. 
2 CONT Year
2 CONT
