1 NAME Theophilus /Redfield/
2 GIVN Theophilus
2 SURN Redfield
2 _MARNM Redfield
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1682
2 PLAC Saybrook (Westbrook)
2 ADDR
3 STAE Connecticut
1 BURI
2 DATE FEB 1759
2 PLAC Old Southwest Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Killingworth
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1759
2 ADDR
3 CITY Killingworth
3 STAE Connecticut
1 OCCU Carpenter, joiner
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Theophilus Redfield==
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH	1682, New Haven, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT DEATH	14 Feb 1759 (aged 76–77), Killingworth, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Old Southwest Cemetery, Killingworth, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA  Show Map, MEMORIAL ID 6192989, Photos by Ray Downing & Howard William Sternberg III
2 CONT
2 CONT Theophilus Redfield, son of James, son of the immigrant William, married Priscilla Grinnell, the great granddaughter of John Alden and Priscilla Mullins. The thirteen children of Theophilus and Priscilla all attained adulthood, an
2 CONC d all had large families of their own. Thus, from Theophilus Redfield come 90 percent of those in the United States today bearing that surname; all of whom may claim Mayflower descendency. {4}
2 CONT
2 CONT "Though never called to take a very prominent part in public affairs, there is evidence that Theophilus Redfield commanded the respect and esteem of the community in which he lived. He was frequently appointed on imporant committe
2 CONC es in the management of town affairs, and at a day when military titles, however humble, had some weight, was known as 'Sargeant (sic) Redfield' "
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT In Memorey of
2 CONT Mr Theophilus
2 CONT Redfield Who
2 CONT Died February
2 CONT Ye. 14th Ad 1759
2 CONT In Ye 77th. Yer.
2 CONT of His Age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandparents
2 CONT William Redfield
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT James Redfield
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT Priscilla Grinnell Redfield
2 CONT 1689–1770
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 13x
2 CONT Daniel Redfield 1707–1758
2 CONT Elizabeth Redfield Hull 1709–1773
2 CONT Richard Redfield b. 6/18/1711, d. 2/2/1771*
2 CONT Ebenezer Redfield 1713–1766
2 CONT Lydia Redfin Leeteb. 2/9/1715/6, d. 12/16/1784*, wife of Benj. Leete 
2 CONT Theophilus Redfield b. 9/6/1718, d. 1/30/1770
2 CONT Priscilla Redfield Bradley b. 7/20/1720, d. 9/7/1799*, Jos. Bradley
2 CONT Peleg Redfield 1723–1760
2 CONT George Redfield 1725–1812
2 CONT William Redfield 12/5/1727–7/1813*
2 CONT Josiah Redfield 1730–1802
2 CONT Jane Redfield Crane 1733–1762
2 CONT James Redfield 3/29/1735–4/3/1797*
2 CONT
2 CONT The gravesites of five of the children of Theophilus are yet undiscovered on Findagrave (see * above)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Reference==
2 CONT
