1 NAME Abraham /Bradley/
2 GIVN Abraham
2 SURN Bradley
2 _MARNM Bradley
2 NICK Bradly
1 NAME Lt. Abraham Bradley
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 MAR 1676
2 ADDR
3 CITY Guilford
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 BURI
2 DATE APR 1721
2 ADDR
3 CITY Guilford
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 APR 1721
2 ADDR
3 CITY Guilford
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 OCCU Military officer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} PER FIND-A-GRAVE #27662444
2 CONT
2 CONT Age 46 yrs 11 mos 8 dys. Surname inscribed on his gravestone as Bradly, but Bradley is the usual spelling in records and genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Bradley I was born in Guilford, Connecticut, on 13 May 1675, according to the Families of the Wyoming Valley by George Brubaker Kulp. His birth date is given as 15 May 1674 in Brief Sketches of a Few American Bradleys, wit
2 CONC h Reference to Their English Projenitors.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of seven children of Stephen Bradley and Hannah Smith. Stephen emigrated to New Haven from Bingley, Yorkshire, England, about 1645 with family and settled in Guilford about 1658.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 Jul 1697 in Guilford, Abraham married Jane Leaming, as recorded in "Brief Sketches of a Few American Bradleys" by John C. Bradley, in Kulp's Families of the Wyoming Valley; in Biographical sketches of the graduates of Yale c
2 CONC ollege; and U.S., New England Marriages Prior to 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham was a merchant, according to the The New England Historical and Genealogical Register. He also was a Lieutenant in the Militia from 1714 to 1721, according to Ancestral Records and Portraits: A Compilation from the Archive
2 CONC s of Chapter I, Colonial Dames of America.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second Abigail Leete about 1719.
