1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''NOTE''': Prior to May 1785, Killingworth was part of New London County, Connecticut. Thereafter, Killingworth became part of the newly created Middlesex County, Connecticut.
2 CONT * Nathan's birth, military, and death information are available on page 18, section 16, of ''Genealogical History of the Redfield Family in the United States'', by John Howard Redfield. Albany, N.Y.: Munsell & Rowland, 1860. Avail
2 CONC able online at https://books.google.com/books?id=Q3hMAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA255&dq=Osbert+Sidney+Comstock&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiZluPLpcuDAxXCrokEHcXpAooQ6AF6BAgKEAI#v=onepage&q=Rufus&f=false
2 CONT * Nathan served in the 4th Company of the 1st Connecticut Regiment. The company was commanded by Captain John Patterson, afterwards commanded by Capatian Roger Enos. The regiment was under the general command of General Lyman and 
2 CONC the special command of Colonel (later General) Putnam. Nathan enlisted on 15 March 1762. He served for thirty-three weeks and four days, for which he was paid 17 pounds, 12 shillings, and six pence.
