1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of ENSIGN.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A094107  DAR Ancestor # A094107]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ambrose Redfield, son of George Redfield and Trial Ward, was born Dec. 13, 1750 in Killingworth, Connecticut. He married on June 12, 1782, with '''LOIS BALDWIN''', dau. of Capt. Caleb Baldwin and Jerusha Parmelee. She was born in 
2 CONC Killingworth, Connecticut on Feb. 1, 1763. She died 1804; he died June 30, 1830. My account is from the Redfield Genealogy, which does not tell where they lived, but likely in New Hampshire, not far from Capt. Caleb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: Heman (1783), Charles (1785), Jane (1787), Caleb (1789), William (1792), Lucius (1795), Ambrose A. (1799), and Wyllis (1801).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ambrose Redfield served as Corporal in Capt, Samuel Gale's Co., part of the 6th Regiment commanded by Col, Samuel Parsons; which served at the seige of Boston as part of Gen. Putnam's Brigade.
2 CONT
2 CONT *See wife Lois' profile for more detailed info on children.
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/baldwingenealogy00baldThe Baldwin genealogy from 1500 to 1881 (1881)
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/genealogicalhist00inredf. Pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT  Author: Baldwin, C. C. (Charles Candee), 1834-1895
2 CONT  Subject: Baldwin family
2 CONT  Publisher: Cleveland, O, [Leader printing company]
2 CONT  Possible copyright status: NOT_IN_COPYRIGHT
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg. 346
