1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Gideon Wellman
2 CONT * Father: William Wellman Jr. 
2 CONT * Mother: Elizabeth Joy   
2 CONT * Birth Date: 2 May 1694 
2 CONT * Birth Location: Killingworth, Middlesex, Connecticut 
2 CONT * Christening Date:  
2 CONT * Christening Location:  
2 CONT * Death Date: BY 4 Jul 1760 
2 CONT * Death Location: prob. Killingworth, Middlesex, Connecticut 
2 CONT * Burial Date:  
2 CONT * Burial Location:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages for Gideon Wellman
2 CONT #Spouse: Concurrence Hull Marriage Date: 14 Apr 1720 Marriage Location: Killingworth, Middlesex, Connecticut
2 CONT #Spouse: Rebecca Grinnell Marriage Date: 13 Feb 1741/1742 Marriage Location: Killingworth, Middlesex, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wellman-848
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sgt William II & Elizabeth (Joy) Wellman
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first Concurrence Hull, daughter of Thomas and Hannah (Sheather) Hull, on 14 Apr 1720 in Killingworth, Middlesex, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gideon Wellman and Concurrance Hull had the following (8) children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuel, b. 21 April 1721
2 CONT # Mary, b. 11 December 1722
2 CONT # Elihu, b. 19 December 1724
2 CONT # Marcy, b. 6 October 1726
2 CONT # William, b. 11 August 1728
2 CONT # Barnabas, b. 17 June 1730
2 CONT # Concurrance (twin), b. 8 September 1733
2 CONT # Lydia (twin), b. 8 September 1733
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (2) Rebecca Grinnell, descendant of John Alden, on 13 Feb 1740 at Killingworth, Middlesex, CT.  No children with 2nd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gideon served in the French/Indian War under Capt. Thomas Pierce in 1760 and again under Capt. Noah Humphry in 1762
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://famouskin.com/family-group.php?name=32021+gideon+wellman&ahnum=1 cites 
