2 CONT Re: Thomas Ingham, b Framington CT 1810 Posted by: Richard G. Temple 	Date: June 02, 2001 at 05:53:02 In Reply to: Thomas Ingham, b Framington CT 1810 by Norman W. Ingham 	of 624
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi,
2 CONT
2 CONT I also descend from the Ingham family. Jonathan Ingham (b. 1727) and Elizabeth Chalker are my 4 great grandparents. Their daughter Deborah (1770-1851), wife of Timothy R. Hawley (1771-1828) are my 3 great grandparents.
2 CONT
2 CONT I am in possession of the transcription of the fifty year diaries of Rev. Rufus Hawley, father of Timothy, above.
2 CONT
2 CONT In those diaries there are three mentions of John Ingham and wife Lois Woodruff, during the late 1700s - 1. On Mar. 4, 1790 Rev. Hawley tells that he married John Ingham and Lois Woodruff. 2. On Oct. 25, 1798, Rev. Hawley mentions
2 CONC  that John Ingham lost a child on Tuesday. 3. On Oct. 26 he mentions that he visited a sick child of John Ingham. On Oct. 27, 1798 he mentions that he visited the children of John Ingham who are sick.
2 CONT
2 CONT Would you happen to have any evidence of the fact that Deborah (Ingham) Hawley was the daughter of Jonathan Ingham and Elizabeth (Chalker) Ingham? I need this proof for entry into Mayflower Society. Elzabeth, through the Chalker f
2 CONC amily, is a Mayflower descendant. Thanks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Temple
