3 STAE NY
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT The first Daniel GRISWOLD, who is most likely to be her grandfather, was born 10 AUG 1728 at Killingworth, Middlesex County, Connecticut; the son of Joseph GRISWOLD and Temperance LAY. Daniel was a Captain in the Infantry. He went
2 CONC  to Havana, Cuba in the War of 1759. He married Lydia HULL about 1750. He was the owner of the mills where the Clinton Paper Manufacturing Company stood. He moved with some of his family to Little Falls, Herkimer County, New York 
2 CONC in 1792. He probably died at Little Falls, Herkimer County, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.themorrisclan.com/GENEALOGY/WEBB%20James%20Henry%20F226.html
