1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LOIS5, Caleb4, Josiah3, Josiah2, John1 (of Milford)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lois Baldwin, dau. of Capt. Caleb Baldwin and Jerusha Parmelee, was born in Killingworth, Connecticut on Feb.1, 1763; m. on June 12, 1782, with '''AMBROSE REDFIELD''', who died June 30, 1830, and she in 1804. My account is from th
2 CONC e Redfield Genealogy, which does not tell where they lived, but likely in New Hampshire, not far from Capt. Caleb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: '''Heman''' (9/13/1783; d. unm. 2/13/1810), '''Charles''' (2/14/1785, of Derry, NH; m. 1814 Elizabeth Adams), '''Jane''' (2/21/1787; m. Luther Keyser), '''Caleb''' (4/19/1789; of Derry NH m. 9/4/1817, Frances C. Coc
2 CONC hran), '''William''' (10/30/1792, of Canada; m. Susan Prentiss), '''Lucius '''(5/14/1795), '''Ambrose A.''' (5/12/1799; d. 5/28/1813), and '''Wyllis''' (9/22/1801, West Clermont NH; m. Martha G. Woods)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Note: Per Redfield Genealogy, she died in Claremont, NH where her parents died. He resided first in Newport after the war, and he died in Derry, NH.
2 CONT
