1 NAME Elizabeth /Wakeman/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Wakeman
2 _MARNM Swift
1 SEX F
1 BAPM
2 DATE 4 MAY 1784
2 ADDR
3 CITY Easton
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 4 MAY 1784
2 ADDR
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1854
2 ADDR
3 CITY Greenville
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} bapt. Easton CT 4 May 1784; d. Greenville GA between 11 Sep 1850 and 6 Feb 1854, prob. Jan 1854. By 1814, she and her husband Nathaniel Swift were living with her parents at Ballston NY; by 1818, her husband was co
2 CONC nsidered mentally ill and was living in the care of his parents at Warren CT. Sometime after the death of her father in 1825, Elizabeth moved with her three children to Georgia, where she spent the remainder of her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 May 1784	Elizabeth Wakeman was baptized at the Congregational Church in Easton, Fairfield County, CT. Before 1796, her father Lloyd Wakeman moved the family to Ballston, Saratoga County, NY, where he and his family joined the 1s
2 CONC t Presbyterian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1809/1810	Elizabeth's younger brother James Wakeman introduced her to a classmate of his at Andover, Nathaniel Swift.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810/1811	Nathaniel Swift and Elizabeth Wakeman were married, probably in Saratoga County, NY (the exact date and place are unknown).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1812-1818	Nathaniel and Elizabeth apparently returned to Ballston NY to live with Elizabeth's parents (her father owned a large and prosperous farm).
2 CONT
2 CONT 24 Jul 1814	Henrietta Swift, Nathaniel and Elizabeth's second child, was baptized at the Ballston Presbyterian Church (Henrietta was born in November 1813).  In the baptismal book, the name of her parent is shown as "Rev. Nathanie
2 CONC l Swift."
2 CONT
2 CONT 1817-1818	Either late in 1817, or early in 1818, Rev. Nathaniel Swift left Ballston NY and returned to Warren CT to live with his parents on their farm. Elizabeth and her children remained in Ballston.
2 CONT
2 CONT 21 Jun 1818	Henry Wakeman Swift, Nathaniel and Elizabeth's third child, was baptized at the Ballston Presbyterian Church ; in the baptismal book , the name of his parent is given as "Mrs. Elizabeth Swift."
2 CONT
2 CONT CENSUS YR:  1850  STATE or TERRITORY:  GA  COUNTY:  Meriwether  DIVISION:  59  REEL NO:  M432-77  PAGE NO:  344B
2 CONT
2 CONT REFERENCE:  G. Bell Blount, September 11, 1850
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ftp.rootsweb.ancestry.com/pub/usgenweb/ga/meriwether/census/1850/pg0341b.txt
